// XFAIL: RT-469: `u8::from(a)` with `let a = 2;` is refused, "cannot convert 'i32' into 'u8': no impl of 'From<i32>' for 'u8'": the variable is typed i32 at the call; the one integer type u8 has a From impl for is u8, and rustc prints 2 (0.30.2)
// From the re-review of the integer-literal work (t302int). Since v0.30.1 at least.
// EXPECT: 2
fn main() {
    let a = 2;
    let r = u8::from(a);
    println("{}", r);
}
